            <ArticleTitle>Wandering spleen with a ten-time twisted vascular pedicle.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>119</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4081/pmc.2016.119</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Torsion of a wandering spleen is a rare cause of acute abdomen in children, usually diagnosed with color-Doppler ultrasonography and enhanced computed tomography. We report a pediatric case of torsion of wandering spleen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
